# SABOTAGE: T170 (bug half) — the THROTTLE clauses are REMOVED from
# `SamenSes.Provider.handle_response/1`, restoring the exact pre-T170 state: an SES
# throttle falls through to the generic `{:ses_error, status, __type, message}` arm. That
# tuple is what the delivery Oban workers hand straight back to Oban, so Oban retries on
# its ordinary exponential schedule — against an account that has just said "maximum
# sending rate exceeded" — and burns one of 20 attempts per hammer.
#
# Flips the named reds in `test/throttle_test.exs`, one per way SES names the condition:
# the SESv2 `429` + `TooManyRequestsException`, the older query API's `400` + `Throttling`,
# and the fully-qualified `com.amazonaws.ses#ThrottlingException`. Each asserts the
# DISTINCT `{:error, {:throttled, seconds}}`; with the clauses gone they get the generic
# SES error back instead. The 400 cases are the load-bearing ones: a sabotage that only
# broke the status match would leave them green.
#
# The POSITIVE CONTROLS in the same file still PASS — a `500` InternalFailure, a
# non-throttle `400` MessageRejected, an error body with no `__type`, a non-map body and a
# `2xx` all keep their exact pre-T170 returns — so the reds fail because the throttle is
# unrecognised, not because SES error handling or delivery broke.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `Samen.Delivery.Throttle` itself (its own reds own that), the
# workers' snooze arms (356 owns that), and the Postmark/Resend adapters (353/355 own
# those). The transport still CARRIES `:headers`, so the plumbing is present and simply
# never consulted.
#
# Removes four contiguous regions (the `Throttle` alias entry, the two throttle clauses,
# and the `generic_error/1` + `throttle_type?/1` + `headers/1` helpers that existed only to
# serve them) so nothing is left unused and the file compiles under
# `--warnings-as-errors`; the two original generic clauses below resume handling every
# error again. Touches samen_ses's provider.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_ses
# TEST_FILES: test/throttle_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: T170 RED: an SESv2 429 TooManyRequestsException is a throttle carrying Retry-After
# MUST_FAIL: T170 RED: the older query API's 400 Throttling is a throttle too, caught by NAME
# MUST_FAIL: T170 RED: a fully-qualified ThrottlingException __type is a throttle
diff --git a/samen_ses/lib/samen_ses/provider.ex b/samen_ses/lib/samen_ses/provider.ex
--- a/samen_ses/lib/samen_ses/provider.ex
+++ b/samen_ses/lib/samen_ses/provider.ex
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 
